    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμότοκ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bringing forth
				immature offspring,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέαινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Cer.</u>
					53
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμοτόκους ὠδῖνας ἀπηρείσαντο λέαιναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Del.</u>
					120
				</span></i>
			 (referring to the shapelessness of the lion cub at birth):
			metaph. of a vine, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.561
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>).</div>
